@title Lesson walk: cooling-what-if (conditions, run, ranked list, apply, check)
@area Learn
# The lesson from the palette, in the hot cabinet sample. Do it for me only carries out commands, so the Cooling what-if button, "Try the fixes" and the Apply button are really clicked. The run takes about a minute (the model runs on a worker thread), so the wait after "Try the fixes" is long. The Apply step scrolls the list to the button by itself (the Heat strip leaves the list a short body at 1366x768); at 1920x1080 the list fits. The fan editor that Apply opens is folded again before the last picture, because it hid half the window.
key ctrl+k
wait 4
text cooling what-if
wait 6
click_text "Fix a hot cabinet: the cooling what-if"
wait 40
shot 01-why
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 02-open-cabinet
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 03-heat-on
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 04-press
check_layout
click_text "Cooling what-if" Button
wait 40
expect "Hottest day outside"
expect "MODEL, NOT MEASURED"
shot 05-conditions
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 06-go
check_layout
click_text "Try the fixes" Button
wait_s 120
expect "Devices over limit"
expect "Model estimate"
shot 07-ranked
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 08-table
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 09-apply
check_layout
wait 20
click_text "Add the openings to Vents and fans"
wait 30
expect "Added a vent"
shot 10-applied
check_layout
click_text "Fan, in the left wall"
wait 10
shot 11-check
check_layout
